Comparative Study: Armature Control vs. Field Control of DC Motor
\f1\b0\fs24 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf2 Task: 
\f1\b0 \cf2 Develop separate Simulink models for armature-controlled and field-controlled DC shunt motor. Compare their dynamic response, speed range, efficiency, and control complexity. Analyze advantages and limitations of each method. Investigate and illustrate (graphically)  constant power and constant torque operation regions. 
\f0\b \cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Importance: 
\f1\b0 \cf2 DC motors can be controlled by varying armature voltage or field current. Understanding both methods and their trade-offs is important for selecting appropriate control strategy.\

\f0\b \cf2 Market relevance:
\f1\b0 \cf2  Field control still used in large industrial motors and traction applications where wide speed range is needed.}